debt_ratchet
  issue 1126
  purpose "Named debt only shrinks. Each ceiling is the measured value at the commit that set it, and a ceiling can only move down, never up. Every measure here names something the architect has actually asked to be removed: prose hardcoded into Rust instead of grounded in the seed (R379), per-case literal string predicates standing in for a rule, and handlers still awaiting migration to data."
  note "Renamed on 2026-09-12. The division of src into a privileged part and the rest was never requested by the architect and is withdrawn: see VISION.md and docs/architect-notes/. The meta-language representation is the system and Rust is one target it is emitted into, so a count of Rust lines measures an output, not the system, and may grow while the algorithm becomes more general. The measure that counted those lines existed only to serve that division and is deleted with it. The literal-predicate measure was scoped the same way and now covers all of src/, which is both simpler and stricter."
  checker "rust-script scripts/check-debt-ratchet.rs"
  release_rule "none. No release depends on any ceiling here. A release is cut on CI correctness alone in .github/workflows/release.yml."
  ceiling
    measure handler_files
    value 46
    how "source rows of data/meta/core-boundary-ledger.lino whose disposition is migrate, other than mod.rs and modules.rs. Promoted generic interpreters are minimal-core machinery rather than specialized handler debt. That ledger is proved equal to the tree, file for file, by scripts/check-minimal-core-boundary.rs, so this is one census and not a second walk."
    note "corrected undercount. 42 counted *.rs under src/solver_handlers/ only, so the four handler files one directory up -- solver_handler_how.rs, solver_handler_how_synthesis.rs, solver_handler_units.rs, solver_handler_oracle.rs -- were invisible, and a migration could have lowered this number by moving a file out of the scanned directory. Issue #1138 B9, plan 09 leaves 1 and 3. No handler was written; the tree is unchanged."
  ceiling
    measure handler_migration_pending
    value 55
    how "occurrences of the phrase status pending in data/meta/handler-migration-ledger.lino, whose census is the live registry: the specialized handler-precedence table followed by the five prelude methods"
    note "corrected undercount. 40 counted the handler-precedence table only, so the five prelude methods -- diagnostic, nl_tool, behavior_rules, feature_capability, playwright_script -- ran on every turn ahead of that table while sitting outside the ledger entirely. Issue #1138 B9, plan 09 leaf 5. Reviewed upward by ten on plan 09 leaf 13: the census now names the ten browser-only rows of handler-precedence.lino (exact_memory_query through software_project_request), which ran in the worker all along while sitting outside the ledger entirely. No handler was written; the tree is unchanged."
  ceiling
    measure literal_predicates
    value 544
    how "occurrences of a contains( or starts_with( call with a double-quoted first argument in src/**/*.rs"
    note "lowered after HTTP provenance checks were generalized from repeated prefix predicates to one parsed scheme predicate (issue #1138, plan 09); reviewed upward by one for the no-memorization ordinary-name exemption's lookup, after the partitive aggregate rule abandoned its three inline reduce_sum/reduce_product literals to read the seed's defined-by reduction edges instead (plan 02 L23/L20); reviewed upward by one more for the live authoring loop's resumable-session protocol check, which must recognize the Agent CLI's ses_ id prefix by shape (plan 03 L13)"
  ceiling
    measure hardcoded_language_rows
    value 1263
    how "non-empty, non-comment rows of scripts/hardcoded-language-allowlist.txt"
  ceiling
    measure authored_ladder_rules
    value 32
    how "*.lino files under experiments/issue_1028_agent_cli_ladder/rules; each is an exact per-leaf edit mapping, so the count is debt and may only shrink"
    note "Issue #1138 plan 03 L15 records the existing 32 mappings without treating them as general capability; the independent rule-disabled ladder result is ratcheted separately once a complete live run exists."
  ceiling
    measure try_dispatch_entries
    value 39
    how "rows of the HANDLER_FUNCTIONS table in src/solver_dispatch.rs whose function name begins with try_. The reading is the one tests/unit/issue_699_handler_migration.rs performs, so the gate and the test cannot disagree about what a dispatch entry is."
    note "Recorded for the first time by issue #1138 B9, plan 09 leaf 4. The number was 39 all along; what did not exist was a checker that would fail when it rose. A Rust constant recorded 50, eleven entries of headroom in which new handlers could be added while every gate stayed green."
  ceiling
    measure promotion_predicates
    value 0
    how "occurrences of the literal handler: prefix in src/intent_formalization/prompt_relevants.rs, one per promotion the prompt formalizer decides in Rust rather than reading from data/seed/handler-promotions.lino"
  ceiling
    measure dispatch_name_special_cases
    value 0
    how "occurrences of a name == comparison in src/meta_method_dispatch.rs plus quoted arms of a name-based runtime match; execution variants are attributes in data/seed/method-execution.lino and the dispatcher branches only on typed attributes"
    note "Reduced from 9 to 0 by issue #1138 B9 plan 09 leaf 12: four comparison sites and the five-arm prelude match now read method-record attributes."
  ceiling
    measure worker_sync_handler_literals
    value 0
    how "name: entries in the unique worker module that defines synchronousHandlerCandidates, discovered by scanning every JavaScript file under src/web/worker. The shipped count is zero because data/seed/browser-handler-precedence.lino owns membership, arguments and order; discovering the owner prevents a moved registry from disappearing outside a fixed-path scan."
  ceiling
    measure store_read_share
    value 4
    how "occurrences of from_store( in src/**/*.rs: the store-reading entry points, which since plan 09 leaf 40 are the backend constructor over an explicit store and LinkStoreSource::shared(), the cached boot accessor every production call site -- run_handler, handler_matches, promoted_relevants -- enters through; plan 09 leaf 41 (stage 3) adds the method registry's constructor and its cached MethodRegistry::shared() accessor, which read the handler table's rank order and the execution and learned-method documents through the same boot projection. This is the one measure here whose strict direction upward is explicit, so a value above the recorded one fails with -lower the reviewed ceiling- and a value below it is the regression. It is a count of entry points and not a percentage, because the value field is an integer and a fraction this plan has not yet run may not be stated as one."
    note "Raised from 1 to 2 by issue #1138 B9 plan 09 leaf 40: the default condition backend flipped from the parsed seed tables to the projected link store, SeedTables was deleted, and every production rule and promotion read now flows through the store accessor. Raised from 2 to 4 by plan 09 leaf 41 (stage 3, the closing leaf): MethodRegistry now enters through the store too -- the specialized table's precedence became rank links the store declares, and the registry's execution and learned-method documents are read as the store's documents, built once behind MethodRegistry::shared() instead of re-parsed per dispatch. The count names entry points, not reads -- after this leaf every routing decision those entry points serve is store-served."
  ceiling
    measure docs_requirements_suites
    value 5
    how "files and directories directly under tests/unit whose names start with docs_, matching tests/unit/docs_requirements/count.rs"
    note "Issue #1138 plan 11 leaf L76 physically nests every retained per-issue suite under one directory while preserving module registration and coverage; the five surviving top-level entries separate benchmark parity, status rendering, issue citations, and the requirement suite's file-plus-directory module surface."
  ceiling
    measure language_parity_gaps
    value 915
    how "lexeme-owning nodes derived from the indentation tree of every data/seed/**/*.lino file that declare at least one en/ru/hi/zh/es lexeme but not all five; each gap must also have one exact dated uncovered_behavior row in data/meta/language-parity-debt.lino"
    note "First structural measurement on 2026-09-17 for issue #1138 plan 11 leaf L75 and issue #949, then lowered from 932 to 930 when the self-use file-analysis repair completed the Spanish workspace audit and verification actions. Lowered from 924 to 915 by issue #1138 plan 08 on 2026-09-20: the Wikidata-grounded membership taxonomy added three genuine hi gaps whose items carry no Hindi label, alias, or sitelink on Wikidata, and the same fetch supplied Spanish surfaces for the eleven entity-name people from Spanish labels and eswiki titles, closing eleven gaps for the three opened. The filename does not decide whether a record is a meaning; direct lexeme ownership does. This is a strict downward measure and may only fall as missing translations are supplied."
